I chose to wish for everyone on Earth to have happiness on their faces, which prioritizes emotional well-being and positivity across the entire planet. I selected this birthday wish because happiness is a universally cherished state that can improve people's lives, even if it's just a temporary moment of joy. The fate tied to this wish (having your face become visible after receiving your wish, and my face being visible as an illustration) adds a magical and immediate visual reward—once people have the happiness written on their faces, they'll be able to see the results. This focus on shared happiness benefits all humanity, and the visual confirmation makes the wish feel real and concrete while maintaining a simple, uplifting narrative. The wish is straightforward and accessible, tying directly to the joy of birthdays and making it meaningful without requiring incantations or symbolism beyond simple arithmetic.

The imagery of eyes being the only change made visible—while being a direct visual indicator of the wish being granted—keeps the person on the ground since the wish involves another party taking responsibility and removing the cost or burden so that everyone and I both get a reward. The wish has a practical effect on the entire worldpop of 7 and keeps the simple narrative thread through to the end with both parties receiving an immediate and symbolic reply. This fulfills the prompt request for a wish that can affect everyone while keeping the entertaining visual narrative cohesive and simple.

